    "knowledge_point": "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function",
    "problem": "If $tan⁡x=16,$ for some value of $x,$ find the value of $\\frac{3}{4}tan⁡(x-9\\pi ).$",
    "worked_solution": "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-9)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $tan⁡x=16,$ we get that $tan⁡(x-9\\pi )=16.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}tan⁡(x-9\\pi )=\\frac{3}{4}(16)=12.\n$$",
